  "name": "collision_course_mix",
  "character": "A wide, dark orchestral cue on one shared space with objects that fly through it: a low organ floor and cello pulse hold the bed, the theme sits in the middle, and the flying parts are placed on the ambisonic bus.",
  "carve_db": -4.0,
  "max_boost_db": 12.0,
  "note": "Carried over from the project 'Antigravity' (every value there was set by a measurement); Starting values: -14 LUFS and -1.5 dBTP follow KB cinematic-hybrid-scoring section 4 (film music mastered at about -14 LUFS: per search result); the crest floor is a working figure; room send per role is the scaffold's, not calibrated. The ambisonic bus is order 4 (25 channels), the shipped value of the other immersive projects; heights follow the instrument presets; stereo_decode speakers because the stereo master is for loudspeakers. The master high-pass is 80 Hz, third order (starting value; with the pedal point held on D2 and A2 the 1 s drift was still 0.00128 at 50 Hz fourth order; drift against a limit of 0.001 was 0.00214 with none, 0.00152 at 30 Hz third order, 0.00121 at 45 Hz third order) from the 34-45 Hz organ pedal; the cinematic reference lists this fix.",
